Deliberate. The architecture requires the observability backend to survive a
primary-side failure, so it is sited where failover lands rather than in the
cluster most likely to fail. aws-primary's collector remote-writes to it over
the interconnect.

Consequence, accepted: if the interconnect drops, metrics from aws-primary stop
arriving. That absence is itself the signal — alert on `up == 0` and on absent()
rather than on values alone.

Not a template for apps/: a workload missing from the standby is a failover
bug. This is a platform component whose placement is the point.
